committer Yuen Su <zypulsecore@gmail.com> 1792307263 +0800

interface: restart shaping when a logical interface changes device

When netifd reports a new l3_device for an active logical interface,
qosify overwrites ifname before calling interface_start(). The latter
returns immediately for an active interface, leaving the old device's
CAKE qdisc and BPF filters installed while the new device is unshaped.
A later down notification then cleans the wrong device.

Stop the active interface before replacing its device name. This removes
the old configuration and lets the existing start path select the right
Ethernet or IP-only classifier for the new device. An unchanged binding
keeps its current qdisc and filters.

Reproduced with complete production interface.c and main.c against real
TC/BPF/CAKE in private network/mount namespaces. Four Ethernet/TUN pairs
exercise eight lifecycle phases each, 64 device checks and 512 IPv4/IPv6
UDP frames with all ECN values. The original fails 32 device checks; the
fix passes all, including old-device cleanup and foreign-filter retention.
Only netifd resolution and pinned program lookup are fixtures; ingress
shaping/IFB, the full daemon and hardware are outside this test.

Fixes: 52a57bf0e4eb ("Initial import")
